WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.120
Just like the long awaited jet packs

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.120
and hoverboards of tomorrow--

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.200
smart contact lenses have been a long time coming.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.780
However, a new way of putting electronics

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.100
into a contact lens is one step closer to making

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.110
contacts that can collect information and display it.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.300
Researchers have created a contact lens

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.660
that monitors glucose levels in tears

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.880
and signals via an LED light.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.040
This could help diabetics do away

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.940
with painful daily blood tests.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:34.280
In the past, contact lenses integrated with electronics

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.440
were stiff and potentially harmful

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.440
to the sensitive human eye.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.920
Here, the components are all flexible

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.980
and, for the most part, transparent.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.340
The graphene glucose sensor, the antenna,

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.760
and the LED are all embedded in a silicon hybrid

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.059
substrate that sits on top of a breathable contact lens.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.600
The lens can stretch up to 30 percent.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.740
And is around 90 percent transparent.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.420
The lens is powered wirelessly through an antenna

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.120
that encircles the pupil, preventing obstruction of sight.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.280
When glucose levels in the wearer rise to

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.200
a predetermined amount,  the LED pixel turns off.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.900
Though this is a good proof of concept, there is still

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.420
a ways to go these lenses haven’t been tested

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.880
in people and there isn’t a practical way to power them.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.560
But with a few improvements,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.180
we could be seeing a lot more with our eyes.

